# Full HMMWV with the REAL steering: a Pitman-arm / idler linkage instead of
# the rack-and-pinion of hmmwv.mech. Everything else -- the free-flying
# chassis, the four double-wishbone corners on shaker posts, the springs and
# shocks -- is identical to hmmwv.mech; only the front steering mechanism
# differs. This is the HMMWV's own steering: Chrono ships it as the default
# (HMMWV_Vehicle.json uses HMMWV_PitmanArm.json), a Pitman arm driven off the
# steering column, a relay ("steering link") carrying both tie rods, and an
# idler arm holding the far end of the relay.
#
# Steering geometry (HMMWV_PitmanArm.json, steering subsystem located at
# [1.24498, 0, 0.101322] on the chassis). Chrono's template is:
#   - Pitman arm: revolute to the chassis (this is the STEERING INPUT), plus a
#     universal joint to the steering link at the arm's outer end.
#   - Steering link (relay rod): the universal to the Pitman arm at one end, a
#     revolute-spherical to the chassis (the idler) at the other, and the two
#     tie-rod attach points along it.
# The Pitman arm and the idler are parallel, equal-length (0.129 m) arms
# swinging about vertical axes, so the linkage is a PARALLELOGRAM and the relay
# rod translates (curvilinearly) as the arms swing -- pushing both tie rods
# and steering the front wheels. This file idealizes that parallelogram to the
# joints the format has:
#   - Pitman arm  -> tree body, revolute z on the chassis (steering input).
#   - Steering link -> tree body, revolute z at the Pitman arm's outer end
#     (the universal joint, idealized to a planar z revolute -- the linkage is
#     planar, so the universal's out-of-plane freedom is unused).
#   - Idler -> a 'distance' loop (length 0.129, the idler-arm length) from the
#     chassis idler pivot to the relay's far end. Because the tree keeps the
#     relay in a horizontal plane, "point on a sphere of radius 0.129" reduces
#     to "point on the idler-arm circle" -- exactly Chrono's massless
#     revolute-spherical idler, with no idler-arm body of its own.
# The steer axis's real ~18.6 deg rearward tilt (the subsystem's orientation
# quaternion) is idealized to vertical, the same axis-aligned idealization the
# wishbone pivots already use. Steering-chain mobility = Pitman arm (1) +
# steering link (1) - idler distance (1) = 1: turn the Pitman arm and the
# relay position, hence both front tie rods, hence front toe, all follow.
# Drive the Pitman-arm joint through its own tau slot (a stiff PD servo on the
# commanded road-wheel/pitman angle), exactly as the posts are driven.
#
# Axes, base frame, hardpoint mapping, mirroring, spring/shock linearization,
# and the free-flying-chassis rationale are all as in hmmwv.mech -- see that
# file's header. Steering points map from the steering-subsystem frame the
# same way suspension points do: add the subsystem location and the +0.026
# wheel-center height shift, i.e. offset (1.24498, 0, 0.127322).
#
# Topology (19 bodies, tree nv 44, nc 33, mobility 11):
#   0  chassis   floating    full HMMWV sprung mass, free-flying (as hmmwv.mech)
#   1  pitman    revolute z  Pitman arm on the chassis -- THE STEERING INPUT
#   2  link      revolute z  relay/steering link, hung off the Pitman arm's
#                            outer end; carries both front tie-rod points and
#                            is held at its far end by the idler distance loop
#   Front-left corner  (3..6), front-right (7..10), rear-left (11..14),
#   rear-right (15..18): each one quartercar (front) or halfcar-side (rear),
#   built exactly as in hmmwv.mech (LCA revolute x, UCA revolute x, spindle
#   floating at the wheel center, post prismatic z shaker).
#
# Loop joints (17): the steering idler (distance) plus 4 per corner x 4:
#   distance   idler: chassis idler pivot -> relay far end, len 0.129
#   per corner: spherical LCA->spindle, spherical UCA->spindle,
#               distance tie rod, distance tire rod (post->wheel, len 0.467)
#   FRONT tie rods run from the STEERING LINK (relay) to the upright steering
#   arm, so relay travel steers them; REAR tie rods run from the CHASSIS
#   (grounded, no steer), as in halfcar.
#
# Mobility 11 = chassis (6, free-flying) + Pitman arm (1) + four posts (4).
#
# q layout (nq 49, nv 44): chassis q[0..6]/v[0..5]; pitman q[7]/v[6];
# link q[8]/v[7]; then each corner LCA(1) UCA(1) spindle(quat+pos 7 / 6) post(1).
# Design pose: q = 0, chassis and every spindle quaternion at identity.

gravity 0 0 -9.81
stab 0.05

body                     # 0: chassis, full HMMWV sprung mass, free-flying
parent -1
joint floating
tree 0 0 0
mass 2086.52
cg 0.056 0 0.239         # HMMWV_Chassis centroid (0.056,0,0.213) lifted +0.026
inertia 1078.52 2955.66 3570.20 0 0 0
fext 1

body                     # 1: Pitman arm, revolute about vertical on the chassis (STEERING INPUT)
parent 0
joint revolute z
tree 1.24498 0.249 0.127322   # Pitman revolute location (subsystem [0,0.249,0])
mass 1.605
cg 0.064 0 0             # arm reaches +x to the universal joint at [0.129,0,0]
inertia 0.00638 0.00756 0.00150 0 0 0

body                     # 2: steering link (relay rod), revolute z at the Pitman arm's outer end
parent 1
joint revolute z
tree 0.129 0 0           # the universal-joint point, in the Pitman-arm frame
mass 3.681
cg 0 -0.249 0           # relay COM; the rod runs -y toward the idler end at (0,-0.574,0)
inertia 0.252 0.00233 0.254 0 0 0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- front-left
body                     # 3: FL lower control arm, pivot y=0.307 z=0.026 (exact x axis)
parent 0
joint revolute x
tree 1.68897 0.307 0.026
mass 23.965
cg 0 0.240 -0.059
inertia 0.4 0.4 0.8938 0 0 0
fext 1

body                     # 4: FL upper control arm, pivot at front/back midpoint
parent 0
joint revolute x
tree 1.53097 0.462 0.2465
mass 5.813
cg 0.052 0.127 -0.0025
inertia 0.03 0.03 0.06276 0 0 0

body                     # 5: FL spindle assembly (upright+spindle+wheel+tire), at wheel center
parent -1
joint floating
tree 1.64897 0.91 0
mass 90.555
cg 0 -0.0342 0           # upright CG sits 0.159 inboard of the wheel center
inertia 4.896 7.581 4.774 0 0 0
fext 1

body                     # 6: FL shaker post pad at the contact patch -- a driver
parent -1
joint prismatic z
tree 1.64897 0.91 -0.467
mass 25
cg 0 0 0
inertia 0.35 0.35 0.65 0 0 0

# --------------------------------------------------------------- front-right
body                     # 7: FR lower control arm, mirror of body 3
parent 0
joint revolute x
tree 1.68897 -0.307 0.026
mass 23.965
cg 0 -0.240 -0.059
inertia 0.4 0.4 0.8938 0 0 0
fext 1

body                     # 8: FR upper control arm, mirror of body 4
parent 0
joint revolute x
tree 1.53097 -0.462 0.2465
mass 5.813
cg 0.052 -0.127 -0.0025
inertia 0.03 0.03 0.06276 0 0 0

body                     # 9: FR spindle assembly, mirror of body 5
parent -1
joint floating
tree 1.64897 -0.91 0
mass 90.555
cg 0 0.0342 0
inertia 4.896 7.581 4.774 0 0 0
fext 1

body                     # 10: FR shaker post pad, mirror of body 6
parent -1
joint prismatic z
tree 1.64897 -0.91 -0.467
mass 25
cg 0 0 0
inertia 0.35 0.35 0.65 0 0 0

# ----------------------------------------------------------------- rear-left
body                     # 11: RL lower control arm, pivot y=0.307 z=0.026 (exact x axis)
parent 0
joint revolute x
tree -1.68897 0.307 0.026
mass 23.965
cg 0 0.240 -0.059
inertia 0.4 0.4 0.8938 0 0 0
fext 1

body                     # 12: RL upper control arm, pivot at front/back midpoint
parent 0
joint revolute x
tree -1.47596 0.462 0.252
mass 5.813
cg -0.089 0.127 -0.005
inertia 0.03 0.03 0.06276 0 0 0

body                     # 13: RL spindle assembly, at wheel center
parent -1
joint floating
tree -1.65297 0.91 0
mass 90.555
cg 0 -0.0342 0
inertia 4.896 7.581 4.774 0 0 0
fext 1

body                     # 14: RL shaker post pad, a driver
parent -1
joint prismatic z
tree -1.65297 0.91 -0.467
mass 25
cg 0 0 0
inertia 0.35 0.35 0.65 0 0 0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- rear-right
body                     # 15: RR lower control arm, mirror of body 11
parent 0
joint revolute x
tree -1.68897 -0.307 0.026
mass 23.965
cg 0 -0.240 -0.059
inertia 0.4 0.4 0.8938 0 0 0
fext 1

body                     # 16: RR upper control arm, mirror of body 12
parent 0
joint revolute x
tree -1.47596 -0.462 0.252
mass 5.813
cg -0.089 -0.127 -0.005
inertia 0.03 0.03 0.06276 0 0 0

body                     # 17: RR spindle assembly, mirror of body 13
parent -1
joint floating
tree -1.65297 -0.91 0
mass 90.555
cg 0 0.0342 0
inertia 4.896 7.581 4.774 0 0 0
fext 1

body                     # 18: RR shaker post pad, mirror of body 14
parent -1
joint prismatic z
tree -1.65297 -0.91 -0.467
mass 25
cg 0 0 0
inertia 0.35 0.35 0.65 0 0 0

# ============================================================ steering idler
loop                     # idler: chassis idler pivot -> relay far end (massless idler arm)
predecessor 0
successor 2
joint distance
ptree 1.24498 -0.325 0.127322
stree 0 -0.574 0
length 0.129

# ================================================================ FL loops
loop                     # FL lower ball: LCA_FL outer end to spindle_FL
predecessor 3
successor 5
joint spherical
ptree -0.036 0.48 -0.118
stree 0.004 -0.123 -0.092

loop                     # FL upper ball: UCA_FL outer end to spindle_FL
predecessor 4
successor 5
joint spherical
ptree 0.105 0.254 -0.0055
stree -0.013 -0.194 0.241

loop                     # FL tie rod: STEERING LINK to spindle_FL steering arm (STEERED)
predecessor 2
successor 5
joint distance
ptree 0.066 0.199 0.035
stree -0.136 -0.089 0.01
length 0.4094604

loop                     # FL driver rod: post_FL pad to wheel center, one tire radius
predecessor 6
successor 5
joint distance
ptree 0 0 0
stree 0 0 0
length 0.467

# ================================================================ FR loops
loop                     # FR lower ball, mirror
predecessor 7
successor 9
joint spherical
ptree -0.036 -0.48 -0.118
stree 0.004 0.123 -0.092

loop                     # FR upper ball, mirror
predecessor 8
successor 9
joint spherical
ptree 0.105 -0.254 -0.0055
stree -0.013 0.194 0.241

loop                     # FR tie rod: STEERING LINK to spindle_FR steering arm (STEERED)
predecessor 2
successor 9
joint distance
ptree 0.066 -0.697 0.035
stree -0.136 0.089 0.01
length 0.4094604

loop                     # FR driver rod, mirror
predecessor 10
successor 9
joint distance
ptree 0 0 0
stree 0 0 0
length 0.467

# ================================================================ RL loops
loop                     # RL lower ball: LCA_RL outer end to spindle_RL
predecessor 11
successor 13
joint spherical
ptree 0.036 0.48 -0.118
stree 0 -0.123 -0.092

loop                     # RL upper ball: UCA_RL outer end to spindle_RL
predecessor 12
successor 13
joint spherical
ptree -0.177 0.254 -0.01
stree 0 -0.194 0.242

loop                     # RL tie rod: CHASSIS to spindle_RL steering arm (grounded, no steer)
predecessor 0
successor 13
joint distance
ptree -1.46596 0.416 0.085
stree 0.134 -0.089 0.017
length 0.4140749

loop                     # RL driver rod: post_RL pad to wheel center, one tire radius
predecessor 14
successor 13
joint distance
ptree 0 0 0
stree 0 0 0
length 0.467

# ================================================================ RR loops
loop                     # RR lower ball, mirror
predecessor 15
successor 17
joint spherical
ptree 0.036 -0.48 -0.118
stree 0 0.123 -0.092

loop                     # RR upper ball, mirror
predecessor 16
successor 17
joint spherical
ptree -0.177 -0.254 -0.01
stree 0 0.194 0.242

loop                     # RR tie rod: CHASSIS to spindle_RR steering arm (grounded, no steer)
predecessor 0
successor 17
joint distance
ptree -1.46596 -0.416 0.085
stree 0.134 0.089 0.017
length 0.4140749

loop                     # RR driver rod, mirror
predecessor 18
successor 17
joint distance
ptree 0 0 0
stree 0 0 0
length 0.467

# ============================================= spring/shock POIs and TSDAs
# Identical to hmmwv.mech except the LCA body indices (front 3/7, rear 11/15).
poi springChassis_FL 0 1.79297 0.51 0.223
poi springArm_FL 3 0.097 0.236 -0.047
poi shockChassis_FL 0 1.79297 0.498 0.349
poi shockArm_FL 3 0.097 0.236 -0.047

poi springChassis_FR 0 1.79297 -0.51 0.223
poi springArm_FR 7 0.097 -0.236 -0.047
poi shockChassis_FR 0 1.79297 -0.498 0.349
poi shockArm_FR 7 0.097 -0.236 -0.047

poi springChassis_RL 0 -1.79297 0.502 0.282
poi springArm_RL 11 -0.097 0.236 -0.047
poi shockChassis_RL 0 -1.79297 0.498 0.349
poi shockArm_RL 11 -0.097 0.237 -0.038

poi springChassis_RR 0 -1.79297 -0.502 0.282
poi springArm_RR 15 -0.097 -0.236 -0.047
poi shockChassis_RR 0 -1.79297 -0.498 0.349
poi shockArm_RR 15 -0.097 -0.237 -0.038

tsda spring_FL              # HMMWV front coil spring, linearized
from springChassis_FL
to springArm_FL
k 181496.15
c 0
l0 0.339

tsda shock_FL              # HMMWV front shock absorber
from shockChassis_FL
to shockArm_FL
k 0
c 19015.5692
l0 0.339

tsda spring_FR
from springChassis_FR
to springArm_FR
k 181496.15
c 0
l0 0.339

tsda shock_FR
from shockChassis_FR
to shockArm_FR
k 0
c 19015.5692
l0 0.339

tsda spring_RL             # HMMWV rear coil spring, linearized
from springChassis_RL
to springArm_RL
k 401043.45
c 0
l0 0.382

tsda shock_RL              # HMMWV rear shock absorber
from shockChassis_RL
to shockArm_RL
k 0
c 36725.2201
l0 0.382

tsda spring_RR
from springChassis_RR
to springArm_RR
k 401043.45
c 0
l0 0.382

tsda shock_RR
from shockChassis_RR
to shockArm_RR
k 0
c 36725.2201
l0 0.382
